REX can be compiled with the Intel compiler (icc and icpc).

Select Intel compilers by setting the standard CMake variables, e.g.:
  CC=icc CXX=icpc ./build-rex.sh $HOME/rex-install Release
or
  cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icc -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpc

By default the backend compiler follows the CMake compiler. To override it:
  -DWITH-ALT-BACKEND-C-COMPILER=<compiler path>
  -DWITH-ALT-BACKEND-CXX-COMPILER=<compiler path>
  -DWITH-ALT-BACKEND-FORTRAN-COMPILER=<compiler path>

Warnings can be adjusted with standard CMake flags, for example:
  -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS='-w'

Information on Intel compiler options:
http://software.intel.com/sites/products/documentation/hpc/compilerpro/en-us/cpp/lin/compiler_c/index.htm
